ntdll: Keep the TEB in x28 and handle faults in the arena.

Darwin zeroes x18 when it preempts a thread, so NtCurrentTeb and the
dispatchers use x28 (WINE_TEB_IN_X28); the dispatcher changes are not
conditional. A store that faults on a blessed arena page is replayed
through the write alias, and reads of the low shared-data address are
emulated. Fault reports dump guest registers and frames
(KITSUNE_FAULT_STACKS, KITSUNE_NO_GUEST_DUMP). signal_arm64ec.c marks
a program's own allocations for ios_app_vm_call and keeps unwinding
when a frame leaves EC code.
